{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The super glue felt useful for small repairs alongside my fasteners and hooks, and the gel would help me apply it precisely.",
    "The nuts connect to my recent fastener purchases, and the casters connect to moving heavy equipment with a hand truck, though neither is an immediate choice without a specific need."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Wire lugs, heat shrink, terminal strips and electrical connectors require wiring work that I do not currently have planned; buying screws and magnetic hooks does not imply that need.",
    "The water tester, concrete grinding wheel and plastic sheet each need a specific project to be useful to me, and my recent purchases give me no reason to start those projects."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat tools and repair supplies as broadly interchangeable, while I care about the particular job an item helps me finish.",
    "My purchases of hardware assortments seem to have been taken as interest in other supply kits, even when their purpose is electrical rather than mechanical."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent purchases center on fastening, hanging and securing things, which makes practical mechanical repair supplies more relevant right now.",
    "Compatibility and immediate usefulness matter: my recent screws are metric, so I cannot assume 5/16-inch nuts will fit, and a hundred-pack needs a clear purpose before I would choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my interest in practical hardware but stretched it into specialized projects I have no current reason to undertake."
}"}
